<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<shacl>
	<id><![CDATA[ValidateModelBBoxes]]></id>
	<!--
		Explanation (SHACL):
		This SHACL shape validates the overall bounding box of the whole model (dataset).
		1. geom:DatasetBBoxShape targets a single node, the graph IRI <https://vng.nl/geometries/>
		   (sh:targetNode).
		2. A SPARQL-based constraint (sh:sparql) runs one query for that node.
		3. A subquery goes over all geometries that have geom:eastings, geom:northings and the six
		   bbox properties (geom:bboxMinX/Y/Z and geom:bboxMaxX/Y/Z). It calculates the global extent:
		   - X: min and max of (bbox X - eastings)
		   - Y: min and max of (bbox Y - northings)
		   - Z: min and max of the bbox Z values
		   The eastings and northings are subtracted, so X and Y are relative to the model origin.
		4. The model is reported as a violation when the total size of the extent is smaller than 1 or
		   larger than 100 on any axis (for example, globalMaxX - globalMinX).
		5. The result message lists the six global values
		   ("Dataset BBox violation: globalMinX=..., globalMaxX=..., ...").
		6. The severity is sh:Violation.
	-->
	<shape uri="validate-model-bboxes.ttl">
	</shape>
</shacl>